  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nA weak shortwave trough will skirt through the northwestern \nU.S. Tuesday and Wednesday, flattening the aforementioned upper\nridge and nudging the monsoonal moisture toward the east. As a \nresult, dry conditions with slight cooling is forecast for mid- \nweek. The southwest U.S. ridge will make a rapid return by \nThursday and Friday, amplifying northward into Canada while a \nPacific trough approaches the West Coast. This pattern will \nsupport rapid heating and the influx of monsoonal moisture once \nagain, with shower and thunderstorm chances increasing by \nFriday.",
